msgid "Prepare versions for each use"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Keep the versions of a model that each use needs.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A model of a study has one *master*, the richest file, and as many "
"*versions* as its uses ask for: a light one for a phone, one for the web "
"and Heriverse, one for a realtime engine. In the graph each version is a "
"version of the same asset, stamped as derived from the master. Its file "
"is named after the model, the use and its triangles, for example "
"``Column_light1@mobile-webxr-2k.glb``. A version for another use, or with"
" other numbers, sits beside the first one; the same version made again "
"becomes a revision of it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio makes the versions with gltfpack, and with Blender and EM Tools "
"when a normal map has to be baked from the master. The jobs run on the "
"bridge, in processes of their own, so EMStudio stays usable. The master "
"is never changed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid "Open the study and switch to the **Archive** workspace."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Stamp the masters first (see :doc:`/how-to/sources/declare-provenance`): "
"a version made from a stamped file is born stamped as derived from it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a tool is missing, EMStudio says so and offers to install it, as an "
"add-on in ``Settings… ▸ Advanced``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Make a version of one model"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Files window on the folder proxies with SU001.glb chosen and the tab "
"Optimise open: Variants of a model with its five destinations, the engine"
" gltfpack, and the button Optimise 1 model → 1 variant."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the **Files** window, mode **Disk**, choose one or more models "
"(``.glb``, ``.gltf`` or ``.obj``) and open the **Optimise** tab of the "
"tools panel."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Under **Variants of a model**, choose the destination: **Preview / "
"catalogue**, **Mobile webXR**, **webXR (ATON / Heriverse)**, **3D "
"printing** or **Desktop realtime (Blender, Unreal)**. The tab says how "
"the geometry, the textures and the compression will be treated, which "
"engine runs, and into which folder the version goes. A version that "
"already exists is not overwritten. **Desktop realtime (Blender, Unreal)**"
" runs in Blender with 3D Survey Collection, an experimental way: it needs"
" the experimental functions switched on in **Settings…**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click **Optimise 1 model → 1 variant** (or the same button with your "
"number of models). A chip follows the job; a click, then a second one, "
"cancels it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The version is registered in the graph as a version of its asset, with "
"its step **LOD generation**. Under **Prepare for a use**, in the same "
"tab, **Diagnose** measures what a model or a ``.blend`` costs for a use "
"(triangles, draw calls, textures, download, GPU memory) and what can be "
"improved, before you make anything."
msgstr ""

msgid "Make the versions of the whole study"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the list of the assets with ``File ▸ Consolidate for…``, or choose "
"**Assets** in the mode menu of the **Files** window, and choose the "
"**Target** (see :doc:`consolidate-for-a-target` for reading the list)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tick the assets to treat and click **Apply and queue**: each one receives"
" the proposal for the target, and the job goes into the queue."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To decide by hand, use the bar **or set:** instead: write the triangles "
"(``2k``, ``2500`` and ``10.000`` are all understood), choose a "
"**texture…** size, a **tool…** and **KTX2**, and click **Set on the "
"selected**. Then click **Put in the queue**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The tools are **Blender: decimate + bake normals**, **gltfpack "
"(meshopt)**, **textures → KTX2 only**, **Obj2Tiles → tileset**, "
"**instances (repeated shapes)** and **leave as it is**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Make a lighter version beside one there"
msgstr ""

msgid "A version already covers its target, but you want it lighter."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the row, click **Shrink…**. The window **Shrink** followed by the name"
" of the asset says what there is now for the target."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Write fewer triangles, or choose a smaller texture (or leave **texture as"
" it is**), and click **Put in the queue**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a file with the new name is already there, choose **New beside it**, "
"which adds ``-2`` to the name, or **Replace**, which makes it again over "
"the file there."
msgstr ""

msgid "Manage the version of a target"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The card of each target, at the top of the **Assets** view, ends with "
"**The version for this target**: how many versions were made for it, how "
"many are reused from other targets, and which assets miss one."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Generate what is missing** selects the assets without a version and "
"queues them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Regenerate** makes again, from their masters, the versions made for "
"this target, and the ones to remake after a master was replaced."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Delete the version…** takes away only what was made for this target, "
"after a preview and a confirmation; the versions reused by other targets "
"stay. It waits until every asset has a master: for those that have none, "
"the card offers **Indicate the master file…** or **Promote the richest "
"version to master**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The deleted files have no undo. The target is then uncovered for those "
"assets, and the master is never loaded in their place."
msgstr ""

msgid "Look after the versions of one model"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the asset with ▸: its versions appear under it, each with its level,"
" its numbers and its textures."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The menu of a version row, **More on this version**, holds **Remove this "
"version…** and, on the master, **Replace the master…**. A new master asks"
" for the path of its file and for the reason, which is kept in the chain;"
" the versions made from the old master are then marked to remake."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the panel on the right, **Versions of** followed by the name of the "
"asset lists the version files on the disk, with their state in the graph."
" Tick **Delete** on the ones to remove and click the button that counts "
"them, for example **Delete the selected (3)**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To remove the versions of one level across the whole study, choose it in "
"the menu **Level: all**, click **Select the visible**, and then the "
"button that counts them, for example **Remove 12 versions…**. A preview "
"and a confirmation come first. The master is never removed from there."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose the version a model shows"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Select a model and open the section **Versions** of the **Inspector**. "
"**Mode** says how the 3D scene chooses: **For the hardware** of this "
"machine (the default), **The lightest**, **Versions: automatic, by the "
"distance**, **By use**, or **Manual**, which keeps the one drawn. "
"**Version** picks one by hand, and **Use of this device** sets the use "
"that **By use** follows. The same modes are in the context menu of the "
"models in the 3D scene, for all the models selected. The hardware profile"
" of the scene is described in :doc:`/how-to/space/load-models-and-"
"tilesets`."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For each model, a master and the versions its uses need, each one a "
"stamped file registered in the graph as a version of the same asset, so "
"that every viewer loads the one made for it."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`consolidate-for-a-target`, to check a target before handing the "
"study on."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`storage`, for the **Files** window and its tools panel."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/explanation/dtc-and-em`, for the chain that links each version to "
"its master."
msgstr ""

